--------------------------------------------------------------------postman assist-------------------------------------------------
Spring Batch REST API - Complete Postman Testing Documentation
📋 API Overview
Base URL: http://localhost:8080/api
This documentation covers all endpoints for the Spring Batch Customer Processing application that reads CSV data, processes it, and provides REST APIs for customer management.
________________________________________
1. 🟢 BASIC CONNECTIVITY & BATCH ENDPOINTS
GET /api/test
Purpose: Basic connectivity test to verify the controller is working
•	Method: GET
•	URL: http://localhost:8080/api/test
•	Headers: None required
•	Body: None
Expected Response:
json
"CustomerController is working!"
What it tests: Verifies that the Spring Boot application is running and the CustomerController is properly mapped.
GET /api/health
Purpose: Health check endpoint to verify API status
•	Method: GET
•	URL: http://localhost:8080/api/health
•	Headers: None required
•	Body: None
Expected Response:
json
"Spring Batch Practice API is running!"
What it tests: Confirms the entire API infrastructure is operational.
POST /api/batch/start
Purpose: Starts the Spring Batch job to process the CSV file and load data into PostgreSQL
•	Method: POST
•	URL: http://localhost:8080/api/batch/start
•	Headers:
o	Content-Type: application/json
•	Body: None required
Expected Response:
json
"Batch job started successfully!"
What happens behind the scenes:
1.	Spring Batch reads customers.csv from classpath
2.	Processes each record through CustomerItemProcessor:
o	Converts names to uppercase
o	Formats phone numbers
o	Standardizes gender and country formatting
o	Attempts to parse various date formats
3.	Stores processed data in PostgreSQL customer_info table
4.	Job completion listener logs the results
Error Response: If CSV file is missing or corrupted
json
"Failed to start batch job: [error details]"
________________________________________
