🚀 RECOMMENDED TESTING SEQUENCE
Step 1: Basic Connectivity Check
text
GET /api/test
GET /api/health
Purpose: Verify the API is running and accessible
Step 2: Data Loading
text
POST /api/batch/start
Purpose: Load and process the CSV data into the database
Step 3: Data Verification
text
GET /api/customers
GET /api/customers/statistics
Purpose: Confirm data was loaded correctly and check initial statistics
Step 4: Filtering & Search Testing
text
GET /api/customers/country/India
GET /api/customers/gender/Female
GET /api/customers/search?name=john
GET /api/customers/domain/gmail.com
Purpose: Test various data filtering and search capabilities
Step 5: CRUD Operations Testing
text
POST /api/customers
PUT /api/customers/1
DELETE /api/customers/1
Purpose: Test create, update, and delete operations
Step 6: Pagination Testing
text
GET /api/customers/page?page=0&size=5
Purpose: Verify pagination works correctly
________________________________________
🛠 TROUBLESHOOTING
Common Issues:
1.	404 Errors: Check if Spring Boot application is running
2.	Empty Responses: Ensure batch job completed successfully
3.	Database Errors: Verify PostgreSQL is running and accessible
4.	CSV Errors: Check if customers.csv exists in src/main/resources/
Log Monitoring:
Watch the console logs during batch job execution for:
•	!!! JOB STARTING! Processing CSV file...
•	Processing: [name] -> [transformed name]
•	!!! JOB COMPLETED! Verifying results...
•	Total records processed: [count]

